{"tool_name":"pigs","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"pigs","home":"http://circe.med.uniroma1.it/pigs/","summary":"Web server for the automatic modeling of immunoglobulin variable domains based on the canonical structure method. It has a user-friendly and flexible interface, that allows the user to choose templates (for the frameworks and the loops) and modeling strategies in an automatic or manual fashion.","addition_date":"2015-01-22T11:49:04Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:21:19.179245Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"version":["1"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:pigs","credit":[{"email":"paolo.marcatili@gmail.com","name":"Paolo Marcatili","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"ELIXIR-ITA-SAPIENZA","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://circe.med.uniroma1.it/pigs/help.php"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Protein sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2976"}}],"note":"Automatic prediction of immunoglobulin structures.","operation":[{"term":"Protein structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0474"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Protein structure","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1460"}}]}],"name":"PIGS","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-ITA-SAPIENZA","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/nprot.2014.189","metadata":{"abstract":"Antibodies (or immunoglobulins) are crucial for defending organisms from pathogens, but they are also key players in many medical, diagnostic and biotechnological applications. The ability to predict their structure and the specific residues involved in antigen recognition has several useful applications in all of these areas. Over the years, we have developed or collaborated in developing a strategy that enables researchers to predict the 3D structure of antibodies with a very satisfactory accuracy. The strategy is completely automated and extremely fast, requiring only a few minutes (~10 min on average) to build a structural model of an antibody. It is based on the concept of canonical structures of antibody loops and on our understanding of the way light and heavy chains pack together.","authors":[{"name":"Chailyan A."},{"name":"Marcatili P."},{"name":"Olimpieri P.P."},{"name":"Tramontano A."}],"citationCount":54,"date":"2014-11-20T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Protocols","title":"Antibody structural modeling with prediction of immunoglobulin structure (PIGS)"},"pmid":"25375991","type":["Other"]},{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btn341","metadata":{"abstract":"We describe a web server for the automatic prediction of immunoglobulin variable domains based on the canonical structure model. The server is user-friendly and flexible. It allows the user to select the templates for the frameworks and the loops using different strategies. The final output is a full-fledged 3D model of the variable domains of the target immunoglobulin. \u00a9 The Author 2008. Published by Oxford University Press. All rights reserved.","authors":[{"name":"Marcatili P."},{"name":"Rosi A."},{"name":"Tramontano A."}],"citationCount":153,"date":"2008-09-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"PIGS: Automatic prediction of antibody structures"},"pmid":"18641403","type":["Other"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0082"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"PIGS","home":"https://bio.tools/pigs","version":"1","summary":"Web server for the automatic modeling of immunoglobulin variable domains based on the canonical structure method. It has a user-friendly and flexible interface, that allows the user to choose templates (for the frameworks and the loops) and modeling strategies in an automatic or manual fashion.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:pigs:1/web/circe.med.uniroma1.it",